From 093899c7ac9ff0838afcc6b03e090b12042ebde9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:03:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 51/52] software_isp: debayer_egl: Add hue, vibrance and a tone
 curve

Compared with a reference phone on the same daylight scenes, the
software ISP's greens came out on the cyan side and dull, its blue
skies on the violet side, and its shadows crushed, which a 3x3 colour
matrix can't correct together without overdoing the reds.

After the colour matrix, in linear opponent space (chroma (B - Y, R - Y)
over the luminance), shift the hue and raise the chroma of each of 12
hue sectors 30 degrees wide, interpolated between their centres: the
dullest colours most (vibrance, falling to none at a chroma limit), and
near-neutral ones not at all. After the highlight shoulder, lift the
shadows with x (1 + a) / (x + a) on the luminance, which keeps full
scale and the hue. The debayer parameters carry the 12 shifts and
vibrances, the limit and the lift; all zero leaves the picture as
before.

Validated with glslang.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
